'''windock†, winnock''' (win′dọk, win′ọk), ''n.'' Same as ''window.'' [Scotch.]
{{smaller block|The foirsaidis—wer diuerss and syndrie tymes callit at the tolbuith ''windok.''
{{right|''Acts James VI.'' (1581), p. 289. (''Jamieson.'')}}
Listening the doors and ''winnocks'' rattle.
